<title>BELGIUM: Cockerill workers on 24-hour strike.</title>
<headline>Cockerill workers on 24-hour strike.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers at Cockerill Sambre downed tools on Friday to protest against planned job cuts.</p>
<p>&quot;After this 24-hour strike we hope that management will return to the negotiating table with a new proposal,&quot; union representative Guy Fayet said in a statement.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the Belgian steel maker was not immediately available to comment on the extent of the strike, which started at 0600 (0400 GMT), or its impact.</p>
<p>Cockerill wants to cut its 7,777 workforce by 2,135 over the next three years, mainly by early retirements. Unions have rejected a proposal to limit the number of redundancies by cutting the working week to 34 from 37 hours.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
